        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "bracelet",
        "stone": "topaz",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Monnaie de Paris"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Within weeks of the Games, athletes posted medals losing their finish.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "real",
        "src": "486-paris-s-olympic-medals-started-chipping-1.jpg",
        "fit": "card",
        "label": "A Paris 2024 bronze",
        "credit": "Public domain, via Wikimedia Commons"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "American skateboarder Nyjah Huston said his bronze was starting to chip.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "stone",
        "stone": "amethyst",
        "cut": "cushion",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Starting to chip"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "French swimmer Clément Secchi said his bronze looked like crocodile skin.",
      "scene": {
        "kind": "piece",
        "piece": "necklace",
        "stone": "emerald",
        "cut": "oval",
        "metal": "yellow",
        "label": "Crocodile skin"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The mint changed its varnish process and offered replacements.",
