  "post": {
    "caption": "Paris's Olympic medals started chipping. The Paris jeweler Chaumet designed the 2024 Olympic medals, and each holds an 18 gram piece of original Eiffel Tower iron. The French mint, Monnaie de Paris, made them. Within weeks, athletes posted medals losing their finish. American skateboarder Nyjah Huston said his bronze was starting to chip, and French swimmer Clément Secchi said his looked like crocodile skin. The mint changed its varnish process and offered replacements, engraved just like the originals. It had made 5,084 medals for the Olympic and Paralympic Games.",
